WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.380
You are watching ColdFusion TV.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.020
Hi, welcome to another ColdFusion video.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:30.220
The human mind is truly an incredible thing, capable of speech, thought, critical thinking, and imagination.

00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:36.558
When we think of the great legendary minds of this world, we think of the brilliance of people like Einstein.

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:42.889
He taught us many things about the low-level rules that govern our universe, fundamental things like time, space and matter,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:50.210
but in terms of practical discoveries that are the basis for the technologies we use each and every day, it was Nikola Tesla.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.410
Who was the most brilliant of all. He had a mind of the rarest kind.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.299
He can memorize entire books and visualize inventions with pinpoint accuracy.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:02.960
Once he had the concept of an invention fully visualized,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:10.280
he then undertook the hard work of bringing it to reality. In comparison, most other scientists and engineers are unwittingly

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.800
narrow-minded in their thinking.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:19.430
How is it that such a man exists vaguely in the public consciousness, only as a fuzzy haze of distant knowledge?

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.979
Today, let's change that.

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:28.039
In this video, you'll learn all about Nikola Tesla and the way he changed the world you live in now.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.680
Let's begin.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:40.240
Tesla of Serbian heritage was born in 1856 in a small village within the Austrian Empire or modern-day Croatia.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.320
Tesla's birth was during a particularly violent lightning storm.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.869
Reading this as a bad omen, the midwife said to Tesla's mother that Tesla would be a child of darkness.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:56.179
Tesla's mom immediately replied: "No, he will be a child of light."

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.840
As we'll see later, this statement was significant.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.340
From an early age, it was clear that Tesla was a remarkable kid.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:12.340
While in high school, he had the ability to perform integral calculus in his head. It was so unusual that his teachers thought he was cheating.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.760
Tesla also possessed an eidetic memory,

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:22.840
which means he could recall entire books and images in great detail — a gift which he attributes to his mother.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:28.200
He allegedly used his imagination to temper visions and vivid nightmares that he had as a child.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.500
Unsurprisingly, Tesla finished high school early.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:40.320
At age 17 though, Tesla had a brush with death after contracting cholera in which he pleaded he might live if his father

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:45.249
let him study engineering instead of the planned path of a priest, or a career in the army.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.900
Tesla's father agreed.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:55.240
Despite being bedridden and incredibly ill at the time, to the astonishment of his family, he miraculously recovered.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:02.420
Keeping true to his agreement, Tesla's father allowed the teenager to study engineering at university.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.780
And the course of history would be changed forever at that moment.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.060
During University in Austria, at age 21,

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:17.860
Tesla got the highest grades possible, could speak eight languages, and was called a star student of the first rank by the University's dean.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.860
Tesla claimed to work from 3:00 a.m. to 11:00 p.m. daily.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:27.900
And because of this, professors wrote a letter to Tesla's father stating that his son may be killed due to overwork.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.980
At the end of his second year, things took a turn.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:39.480
Tesla lost his scholarship and became addicted to gambling, and by his third year, Tesla had gambled away his entire allowance and tuition money.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.860
He did, however, manage to gamble back the losses and return the balance back to his family,

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.880
but the damage to his studies had been done.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:52.180
When exam time came around, Tesla was unprepared and asked for an extension to study, but he was denied.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.660
He never graduated from the University and did not receive grades for his last semester.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:06.900
In December of 1878, to hide the fact that he had dropped out of university, Tesla cut all ties with his family.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:11.940
It was so sudden that his friends had thought he had drowned in a river in North Croatia.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.460
In 1880, he moved to Budapest and then finally to America with just four cents in his pocket.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:27.039
After taking up a few odd jobs here and there, Tesla began his work for Thomas Edison at consciente Edison company, in 1882.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.050
Here's a word on Edison:

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:33.820
Many people today consider Thomas Edison as the father of the light bulb,

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:37.220
but he was more along the lines of the Steve Jobs of the light bulb.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:43.680
That is, Edison figured out how to sell the light bulb by improving on ideas of 22 other men before him.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:51.060
Thomas Edison went on to found General Electric, which I also have a video on, so if you want to see that, check the description below.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.340
Okay, so back to this story.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:05:00.100
In 1885, Tesla said that he could redesign Edison's DC motors and generators

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:04.480
which were very inefficient at the time, and had a tendency to spark and break down.

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:10.630
Edison liked the idea and offered Tesla 1 million US dollars in today's currency for the job.

00:05:11.419 --> 00:05:15.848
Tesla got to work and did as he was promised, fixing all the problems with the motors.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:21.480
The new motors and generators were now simpler, didn't spark, and were much more reliable.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:28.300
In fact, Tesla's design was so good that it still used today for the motors that power anything from household appliances,

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:35.340
to water pumps, power tools, disk drives, smartphone haptics feedback systems, and, of course, the Tesla electric car.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.920
When Tesla had completed this job and asked for the money, Edison laughed and stated:

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.440
"Mr.Tesla, you do not understand our American humor."

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:50.470
Tesla had just been ripped off big time, and left Edison's company. He'd had enough.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:58.060
Meanwhile, at this time, something monumental was happening: the electrical revolution was just about to take place.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:04.040
Electricity was the next big thing to change the entire planet. It created an investment startup bubble,

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:07.920
much greater than the fever that was the dot-com bubble of the 1990s.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:16.260
Billion dollar industries arose out of nowhere, and the American economy was lifted into an enhanced growth period that would last for decades.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:22.660
This was due to sudden quantum leaps in manufacturing, household technology, and general efficiency of work.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:28.140
Work and life was simply easier. We simply just can't comprehend this change today.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:35.200
Why, you might be asking. Because everyone alive today was born with electricity. The sheer magnitude of

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.960
technological change that resulted from household electricity was truly astonishing

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:51.380
So, after being cheated by Edison, Tesla decided to put his energy into joining the electric revolution in the form of the research of alternating current, or AC.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.880
While he searched for financial backers to support his vision of an AC powered world,

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:03.160
Tesla took up a job of digging ditches for $2 a day, or $50 in today's currency to make ends meet.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.959
He described this period as very painful.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.800
Tesla eventually struck up a partnership with Westinghouse.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:17.300
This would put him in direct competition with Edison and his direct current or DC system backed by General Electric.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:22.860
Edison's DC system created dangerous sparks, couldn't transmit electricity very far,

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.180
required a power plant every few kilometers with cables as thick as your arm.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:31.780
In other words, it was pretty terribly suited to power every home on this planet.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:39.780
Tesla's AC system, on the other hand, used thinner wires, had higher voltages, and could transmit electricity over long distances.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:44.860
The fight was on, and the prize for the winner was the privilege of lighting up the entire world.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:49.200
By 1893, there had been many shady business deals,

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:53.600
stolen ideas and patent suppression that Edison and his money interests

00:07:53.600 --> 00:08:01.040
wielded over Tesla's inventions. The feud had reached boiling point, and with this, the war of the currents had reached its peak.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.869
Deep down, Edison knew that his system was inferior to Tesla's.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:16.100
But, of course, he didn't want the public to know this. He needed a way to make the public despise AC and accept DC.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:17.920
But how?

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:25.440
Families living near Edison's laboratory began to notice something a little strange. Their pets suddenly began to disappear

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.300
These mysterious disappearances weren't the work of aliens,

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:35.900
but of a group of schoolboys paid 25 cents for each animal that they stole. This was Edison's solution.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:41.200
Once Edison gathered the cats, dogs, and other animals from the school boys,

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:49.480
he publicly electrocuted them using Tesla's AC current to prove that it was dangerous, too dangerous to be used in any home. In addition to this,

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:54.979
Edison aided in the creation of the electric chair making sure that it used AC current.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:09:02.260
Tesla responded to all of this by demonstrating that AC was perfectly safe by famously shooting electric current

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:06.960
through his own body to produce light at the 1893 World Fair.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.840
This was checkmate to Edison and a symbolic turning point.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:18.400
As the years went on, AC increased in popularity and became the standard due to its technical advantages.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:26.820
As a result of his inventions, Tesla was shot into the stratosphere of stardom, rubbing shoulders with the most important people of the day.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:31.580
He was universally loved by citizens because he helped to make their lives easier.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:36.640
From arriving with just four cents in his pocket to now have an unprecedented fame,

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:41.440
things have certainly changed for Tesla, and his brilliance and hard work had paid off for him.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:50.540
Meanwhile, Edison became more and more despised by others within General Electric and eventually lost control of the company after a series of mergers.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.740
With all of that being said, to give Edison some credit,

00:09:54.740 --> 00:10:00.770
he did invent the phonograph and motion picture camera, so he also has contributed greatly to society.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:09.240
During the War of the currents, Tesla designed AC motors, generators, transformers, and power transmission

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:15.280
technologies, resulting in 25 of the most valuable patents since the invention of the telephone.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:21.580
These designs were so good that we still use them today in all the systems that power our homes,

00:10:21.839 --> 00:10:23.839
a fact which we take for granted.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:30.120
This in itself was an incredible achievement by Tesla, but he was just getting started.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:39.140
Over the next few years, Tesla would invent a few foundational technologies that drove the 20th century and still hold relevance today.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:43.039
We'll take a look at that in a second, but before we do,

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:48.440
I think it's time for a quick break, so grab a bite to eat get comfortable, readjust, and we'll be back in a bit.

